(#:card{:code "macr",
        :collector-number "1",
        :name "Into the Story: Assassin Edition // Story Beats",
        :layout "double_faced_token",
        :highres? true,
        :layout-category :transform,
        :faces
        [{:png
          "https://cards.scryfall.io/png/front/6/f/6f98df20-e932-47a5-ba0c-ba17c0e11df0.png?1729216153",
          :type-line "Card",
          :oracle-text
          "OBJECTIVE:\nCreate your own Assassin's Creed storyline, using the cards in your boosters as inspiration.\nGET READY:\nOpen two boosters for each player and remove any cards without magic card backs.Then sort the cards into separate piles for creature cards, land cards, and other noncreature cards. Shuffle the piles and place each of them face down.\nLET'S PLAY:\nGo through the beats of the other side of this card in order, revealing a card from the top of the specified pile or taking the specified action. Tell a story as you go. After a player tells a bit of the story for a beat, it's the next player's turn for the next story beat. If there are no cards of the requested type, players can make something up."}
         {:png
          "https://cards.scryfall.io/png/back/6/f/6f98df20-e932-47a5-ba0c-ba17c0e11df0.png?1729216153",
          :type-line "Card",
          :oracle-text
          "INTRODUCTION\n• Setting: a land\n• The protagonist: a creature\n• Why the protagonist is at the location: a noncreature card\n• The villain: another creature card\nACTION\n• The protagonist recruits allies: two creature cards\n• The protagonist and allies get stronger: a noncreature card\n• Take down the henchman: a creature card and a noncreature card\n• An unavoidable death: choose one of the allies\n• Describe the villain's weakness/secret/motivation and how the allies discovered it: a noncreature card or a creature card\nRESOLUTION\n• Confronting the villain: a noncreature card\n• The final assassination: choose one of the allies and a noncreature card\n• Ending: Create this yourself! What did the protagonist do after the assassination? Did they get what they need? Was it worth it?\nTO WIN:\nAfter the story's been told, assign the following awards by popular vote to players: Coolest, Funniest, and Most Historically Inaccurate. Feel free to invent your own awards as well. In the case of a tied vote, determine the winner of that award randomly."}]}
 #:card{:code "macr",
        :collector-number "3",
        :name "Find the Assassin // Find the Assassin (cont'd)",
        :layout "double_faced_token",
        :highres? true,
        :layout-category :transform,
        :faces
        [{:png
          "https://cards.scryfall.io/png/front/9/5/952ae479-8b0c-4aec-8daa-653a4fecec50.png?1734842916",
          :type-line "Card",
          :oracle-text
          "2+ players | 2 packs | 5 minutes\nOBJECTIVE:\nWork together to score as many points as possible by deciphering your teammates' clues and correctly guessing the mystery card.\nGET READY:\nOpen two boosters and remove cards without Magic backs. Separate into a pile of creatures and a pile of noncreatures.\nLET'S PLAY:\n• Each round, turn the two piles face down and shuffle them. Then determine which player was assassinated. That player is the clue-giving ghost for the round. The ghost is not allowed to communicate with the other players, except as directed.\n• The ghost looks at the top card of the creature pile. That is the assassin who killed them. Shuffle the cards in the creature pile and reveal them. Then reveal three random cards from the noncreature pile. The ghost chooses one of the noncreatures as a clue. (Try picking a card with similar art or theme to the assassin!)"}
         {:png
          "https://cards.scryfall.io/png/back/9/5/952ae479-8b0c-4aec-8daa-653a4fecec50.png?1734842916",
          :type-line "Card",
          :oracle-text
          "• Now, each other player picks which creature they think is the assassin based on that clue. Each player who picks the right assassin gets 1 point. The ghost also gets 1 point unless none of the other players picked the right assassin.\nTO WIN:\nKeep playing until every player has been the ghost once. At the end, the player with the most points wins!"}]})
